FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after the existing recipe patches. Found by the deterministic simulation in sim/redoxfs (sim/redoxfs/run.sh replay FILE runs a replay).

Renaming a directory into itself or into one of its descendants was not refused: it either failed with ENOTEMPTY or detached the subtree into a cycle no path reaches. rename_node and rename_node_no_replace now return EINVAL, as POSIX requires.

Replay (seed 1): mkdir /g3; rename /g3 /g3/h returns ENOTEMPTY instead of EINVAL; with a deeper target the rename succeeds and leaks the subtree. Without this patch 120 of 120 simulated seeds fail.
